  "about": "Loop points of the story v2 town and train loops (seconds and samples at 44.1 kHz, in the decoded MP3). Play the file once from 0, then loop [loopStart, loopEnd): WebAudio AudioBufferSourceNode.loop with loopStart/loopEnd. The file runs 0.5 s past loopEnd (the song's own continuation, faded out) so the MP3's end-of-file edge never touches the seam: use the loop points, not a whole-file loop. Times assume the decoder honours the MP3's gapless header (Chrome and Firefox do; decodeLag 0 is ffmpeg's decode against the pre-encode audio). seam: three loops rendered back to back from the decoded MP3; click_ratio is the sample jump at each seam over the 99.9th percentile of jumps within 250 ms (under 1 means no click), hf_spike_ratio the largest high-passed (above 6 kHz) sample within 0.5 ms of the seam over the 99th percentile within 50 ms around it (about 1 or under means no spike), phase_shift_ms the onset grid phase after the seam minus before (tempo hitch).",
